WEBVTT

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:12.030
Take wing and gather together.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.200
The festival of stars is nigh.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.610
You're amazing!
The festival of stars is nigh.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.740
It's the rookie we've been hoping for.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.660
-Keith.
-Didn't you even know that?

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:08.920
Is she dead?

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.300
Nope, she's still alive!

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.760
Then hurry up and get started!

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:18.300
Sure.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.140
Let's clean our kill.

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:44.070
Henry! Richard!

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:15.650
Kingdom of Cremona, Old Town

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:37.250
Hey! Freshly baked buns!

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:52.310
Oh crap!

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:54.810
Good morning, Lily.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.020
Morning, Koku!

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:57.060
Um, would you-

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.990
Sorry, I'm running late!
Um, would you-

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:00.440
Maybe next time!

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:06.030
But these are freshly baked red bean buns.

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:18.800
Mom! Mom! I forgot my ID!

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.260
What are you doing, you idiot?

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:30.930
This is 105. Homeless man's tent
located off the forest road.

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:32.050
This is 112.

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:35.360
Bloodstains found in parking lot.
Leaving them for the CSI.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:39.760
Good morning, ma'am!

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:41.280
Shh!
Good morning, ma'am!

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:46.780
Good morning!

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.410
Hey. You're late.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.120
Er, sorry about that.

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:54.750
Want a red bean bun? Freshly baked!

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:58.170
You can eat at a crime scene?
How impudent.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.510
So, are the victims more... you know?

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.050
We linked our vics to multiple murders
in our jurisdiction.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:11.760
We had them pegged as serial killers,

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:19.100
but before we could get an arrest warrant,
our misguided pal got to them.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.110
Killer B.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.040
It's fine, shut up.
I'm sorry, sir, this area is-

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:35.180
Shoo.

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:36.210
Sir, I insist...
Shoo.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.080
Hey! Who the heck is that?

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:40.880
Er, he said he's with the RIS.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.040
I don't know him!

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.170
You can't let an outsider in here!

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.010
Excuse me. I need your attention.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:52.350
This area is currently off-limits to all
but authorized personnel.

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:58.140
Mister? Are you drunk?

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:01.020
Civilians aren't allowed in--

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:07.280
How have you been, Genie!
It's been a while!

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:08.900
"Genie"?

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:12.240
Eric and Jean are dying to see you!

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:14.700
You should go see them!

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.040
Hey.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:31.220
Royal Police, Coastal Branch

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:39.190
That covers pretty much all of the intel
we have so far. As for the rest...

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:43.570
Wow. It's really Keith Flick, Mario!

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:51.280
He's just an old has-been
who's been gone for 10 years.

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:54.300
Eric, everything's ready.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:55.080
Good.
Eric, everything's ready.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:06:01.540
Before we begin, let me introduce someone.
Everyone, look to your two o'clock.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:06.840
The man standing next to Jean
is Keith Flick.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:11.550
As of today, he's rejoined our unit from
the Archives Division. Let's welcome him.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:13.010
Hey.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:14.840
Okay, Kaela. Begin.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:21.480
Early this morning, multiple bodies
were found in the forest area.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:24.190
The victims are the Crouse Brothers,
Henry and Richard.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:27.280
Both were killed
with a sharp, bladed weapon.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:32.240
An unconscious woman was also found.
She's been hospitalized for her injuries.

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:36.200
We've confirmed that the Crouse Brothers,
including the youngest, Julian,

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:39.460
-abducted, imprisoned, and raped her.
-Another psychopath, huh?

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:43.290
Speaking of whom,
Julian Crouse's whereabouts are unknown.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:50.050
Kill!

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:52.010
Kill!

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:54.800
Kill! I'm gonna kill him!

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:02.520
Kill! Kill! I'm definitely gonna--

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.640
I can arrange a meeting.

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:10.270
If you help me out
with one teeny, tiny thing.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:14.860
So, who killed these criminals?

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:18.030
The RIS's job will be to focus on this.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:21.160
Commonly known as "Killer B."

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:24.130
This is the lead suspect
we will be pursuing.

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:28.300
I wish they'd call him
"The lousy misguided scumbag pal."

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.050
You added "lousy" and "scumbag."

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:34.800
We believe he has been involved
in 15 killings over the past few years.

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:37.260
Mario, present your report.

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:41.270
We've gone over this before,

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:44.730
but since we have a newcomer,
I'll run through it again.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:49.100
Cause of death,
single blow from sharp blade.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:50.440
No defensive wounds.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:55.910
This means our perp sneaks up and
cuts his victims before they can cry out.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:58.910
It's certain that this guy is no amateur.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:00.790
Brandon. Do you have a profile?

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.290
I've been working it from various angles,

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:05.790
but without any keywords
to narrow it down,

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:08.460
there's no way
to make it any more accurate.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.000
How about the mark?

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.050
Kaela, can you put it up?

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:13.510
Hang on.

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:18.470
There's a countless number
of similar ones. It's just a "B."

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:21.390
My eyes are dazzled.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:25.390
He's even got fan sites?

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:26.850
I guess he's popular.

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:29.270
I've got a whole lot more.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:31.810
Keith.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:37.530
When you look at this,
does anything jump out at you?

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:41.830
Asleep, weren't you?

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:46.000
Kaela, put up those other images.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.990
Sure. Want them all?

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:50.200
Just don't dazzle Boris' eyes.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:51.960
I don't think that's possible.

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:04.140
What happened? Hey!

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:23.950
I agree.

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:27.870
You sure got old.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:30.870
Genie.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:34.540
There aren't any ashtrays.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.670
Everywhere's no-smoking these days.

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:39.470
I quit smoking, too. Quite a while ago.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:45.680
This bitter swill sure takes me back.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.060
Don't drink it, then.

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:56.480
It's the anniversary of her death, huh?
The year flew by.

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:57.450
Yeah.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:10.500
Hard at work right after getting back,
I see.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:13.370
If you ever want bad coffee,
come by anytime.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.000
Sure.

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:19.670
Oh, almost forgot.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.100
He knew I was lying?

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.490
Assistance requested
by army and municipal police!

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:45.200
Someone's attacking an army convoy!

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:50.410
They've stolen an IFV and are now fleeing
towards the capital on the Aqua Line!

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:52.670
The royal family has declared martial law!

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:55.380
What's this?
We're to obey Gen. Bern's instructions!

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:57.210
Is this a revolution?

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:59.090
Everyone, get there ASAP!

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:01.340
-Mario! Take command on scene!
-Roger!

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:04.180
Brandon, you're our liaison
with the local cops!

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:05.380
Roger!
Boris!

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:08.730
Could you handle the army?
Please oversee our unit placement!

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:10.400
Wait, you want me to do it?

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:11.350
Yes, you!
Wait, you want me to do it?

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:12.940
All right, fine.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:13.700
Keith.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:14.360
What?
Keith.

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:17.480
There's an emergency.
I'd like your assistance.

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.970
You flies are getting on my nerves!

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:46.850
This looks like trouble.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.970
Lily! We're gonna get behind it!

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:50.940
Can you get ahead of or next to it?

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:51.810
Uh...
Can you get ahead of or next to it?

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.220
Cut through the park!

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:54.940
Rodger Dodger!

00:11:55.350 --> 00:11:57.310
W-Wait, Lily! Don't--

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:03.150
I didn't mean it literally!
Use the road! The road!

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:04.900
Target acquired!

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:06.870
Lily!

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:08.990
Here we come!

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:23.380
Lily! It's firing at us!

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:24.340
Sorry! Falling back!
Lily! It's firing at us!

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:27.090
Lily!

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:34.060
We can't get near it with this car!
You get ahead of it!

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:36.520
Where is he? Come on out!

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:42.560
Show yourself, you monster!

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:55.280
Die!

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:58.290
I'll crush you all!

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:01.840
This guy is nuts.
I have no idea what his objective is!

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.760
We're not letting him get away!

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:08.680
Julian, I hate to interrupt
while you're having fun,

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:11.260
but it's time to lose them.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.060
Hey, Mario!

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:21.320
Watch the sensors!

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:25.730
A smoke screen and an APS?

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:28.360
This isn't an ordinary IFV?

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:30.490
It probably contains
carbon fiber particles.

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:34.370
Radar waves are being jammed.
Unable to monitor situation.

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:35.640
Anything on thermal?

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:36.460
Not a thing.

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:41.750
Seal off all areas immediately.
Just get that thing contained.

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:44.460
This is Alpha!

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:48.010
Eric! Where'd the IFV go?
Requesting instructions!

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:54.350
Damn it.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:57.310
Who are these people?

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:08.730
Who were they?

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:11.450
Hey, where are you taking me?

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:15.070
Changing rides.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:18.160
The fun is just beginning.

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:20.560
Any sign of the IFV?

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:21.540
Nothing yet.

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:23.580
Where did it vanish to?

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:25.630
I'll boost the satellite's sensitivity.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.590
It's pointless. Pointless.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:33.470
I don't think you'll find them. Probably.

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:37.810
Kaela, can we see
when the IFV entered the tunnel?

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.060
Sure.

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:42.360
Show me again.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:45.730
Let it loop for a while.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.490
Oh, I get it. That's...

00:14:54.690 --> 00:14:58.040
It's a hybrid IFV
that hasn't been made public yet.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:01.460
That sound is the high-pitched tone
an inverter makes.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.460
That's why it suddenly vanished
from the thermal.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:08.420
It's a new IFV with stealth capabilities
pushed to the limit.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:11.550
I remember reading about this somewhere.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:14.930
It's a cutting-edge IFV made
by our undeveloped military,

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:16.970
independently and in top secret,

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:19.640
free from meddling from other countries.

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:21.640
Known as the 5-0.

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:29.110
They effortlessly steal a top-secret item,
and after causing a childish ruckus,

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:32.820
they exploited its capabilities
and vanished.

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:36.620
A fool's prattling, or a wise man's words?

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.660
Either way, this is tricky.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:42.660
Now then.

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:49.420
Which one is the real objective?

00:16:05.470 --> 00:16:07.310
What is that man doing?

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:11.150
What are all those weird squares
and triangles?

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:15.320
As I recall, he called it something like
the variable separation method.

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.030
If you don't know, fine.

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:20.450
I've known him for 20 years now.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:24.160
And I've never known what was going on
in his head!

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:26.120
That's nothing to brag about.

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:27.080
It's just...

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:31.010
if you give him time, he'll show the way.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:32.970
To what?

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:34.420
The answer.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:42.100
Diversion or robbery? Neither.
A diversion to facilitate a robbery.

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:46.350
Two above, below, one above...

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:49.770
Eric.

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:51.650
Hey! The monitor!
Remember this place?

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:53.690
That's a monitor! It's expensive!

00:16:55.230 --> 00:16:57.440
The grounds of Oris Heavy Industries?

00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:00.370
And what's beneath it?

00:17:00.650 --> 00:17:03.080
The abandoned Alpine Metro line.

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:06.290
It connects to the trans-island railway!

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:13.880
The summit's station
is now the Museum of Flight.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:29.690
Alpha! Go to the old Alpine Metro line's
starting station.

00:17:29.970 --> 00:17:32.310
Beta! Get to the Museum of Flight!

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:37.150
Kaela, alert the military, too.
Have them keep an eye on the skies!

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:38.110
Roger that!

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:45.620
Please respond.

00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:48.750
Train 645, this is railway police!

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:51.000
Please respond, train 645!

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:57.970
He's really going to show up, right?

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:00.840
Because if you're lying...

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:06.060
Message from railway police!

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:09.020
Runaway freight train
on National Rail loop line two!

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:10.430
Shall I divert Alpha?

00:18:10.430 --> 00:18:14.350
Ignore it. The police and army
will home in on that, anyway.

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:16.980
The IFV isn't on it.

00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:20.160
The fool who's hard at work
on that freight train

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:23.330
will be made out to be the perpetrator
when it's over.

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:25.820
Just wait for it to stop.

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:27.200
He's here.

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:35.960
You!

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.300
Is it you?

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:40.590
You really came!

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:41.880
Hey, you--

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:48.100
Thank you for your hard work.

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:00.110
He showed up?

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:01.070
Yes.

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:03.030
Is it him?

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:06.490
If Quinn doesn't return,
we'll know for sure.

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:18.880
I've been ordered
to offer you an invitation.

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:24.800
This is a human that I'm allowed to kill.
He deserves to die.

00:19:25.210 --> 00:19:29.020
Oh, I understand! It's sudden,
and now's not a good time for you!

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:31.480
So that's why...

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:34.980
I'm gonna "invite" you
in my own special way!

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:38.650
They found us sooner than expected.
We'll leave that behind.

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:40.530
Huh? After all this trouble?

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:42.190
The gas?

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:43.190
Got it all.

00:19:44.270 --> 00:19:46.320
We're switching to plan B.

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:47.990
Minatsuki. What about Quinn?

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:50.450
Plan B, he said.

00:19:53.030 --> 00:19:55.330
In other words, we abandon Quinn.

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:58.170
Understood.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:04.050
Hey! What's the matter?
Show me your skills! Your power!

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:06.220
The real you! Come on!

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:18.650
If you have no penitence in your heart,
atone for your sins with your death.

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:30.540
Lohengrin.

00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:33.330
The black-winged king.

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:37.330
He exists.

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:43.500
He really exists, Minatsuki!

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:47.380
Li- Li- Lily!

00:20:47.380 --> 00:20:49.380
Don't talk, you'll bite your tongue off!

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:57.230
Boris, sorry!

00:21:01.180 --> 00:21:02.150
Don't move!

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.120
What's going on?

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:18.460
Don't be in such a rush!
Let's enjoy ourselves a little!

00:21:19.950 --> 00:21:21.630
Oh, wow!

00:21:22.410 --> 00:21:26.220
Still, I just need to make sure
you don't hit me!

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:29.390
I'll take that arm of yours!

00:22:40.370 --> 00:22:42.620
I guess I misread this.

00:22:44.660 --> 00:22:46.670
This was the main objective.

00:23:01.970 --> 00:23:04.190
"Case is closed," huh?

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:06.100
Like hell it is!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:08.280
They're gonna say the train overturned

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:11.310
and the IFV was ditched
in the mountains!

00:23:11.310 --> 00:23:12.490
I don't doubt it.

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:15.320
That story is more convenient
for all involved.

00:23:15.320 --> 00:23:16.340
This is so damn fishy!

00:23:16.340 --> 00:23:16.580
Ow!
This is so damn fishy!

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:17.280
Ow!

00:23:17.610 --> 00:23:19.200
What are you doing, Bran?

00:23:19.200 --> 00:23:20.160
Look at this!

00:23:22.780 --> 00:23:23.790
Hey, that's...

00:23:24.120 --> 00:23:25.090
It can't be.

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:29.090
Come on, it's just a coincidence.

00:23:29.370 --> 00:23:31.130
Yeah, it must be.

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:36.760
Are you seeing my marks?

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:42.310
I'll keep on killing.

00:23:44.010 --> 00:23:46.650
Until you find me.

00:23:52.270 --> 00:23:53.440
I found you.

00:23:56.230 --> 00:23:57.780
I'll find you.

00:23:59.780 --> 00:24:00.780
I'm...

00:24:03.830 --> 00:24:04.830
right here.

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:11.600
Someday I’ll be gone

00:24:13.500 --> 00:24:20.200
To somewhere that we belong

00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:25.580
And god has never played his role

00:24:25.580 --> 00:24:29.860
Because I’m the one who saves my soul

00:24:30.220 --> 00:24:35.000
It is a perfect world we’re longing for

00:24:35.640 --> 00:24:38.140
So long...

00:25:04.930 --> 00:25:08.760
Cursed shadows haunt and gather

00:25:08.760 --> 00:25:12.400
In the city of no answer

00:25:12.780 --> 00:25:16.700
as we follow endless questions

00:25:16.700 --> 00:25:20.620
hands up in the same reflection

00:25:20.910 --> 00:25:24.540
just used to be
Sometimes we try to feel how things

00:25:24.540 --> 00:25:28.680
in yesterdays

00:25:28.960 --> 00:25:32.740
No one ever make it better, no one ever lives forever

00:25:32.740 --> 00:25:36.140
Wake me up and let me go

00:25:36.560 --> 00:25:44.340
Someday I’ll be gone

00:25:44.340 --> 00:25:50.440
To somewhere we all belong

00:25:50.440 --> 00:25:53.200
For so long
